.TH "EPX\-CHANGELOG" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-changelog \- read the change history (audit log)
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx changelog [flags]
epx changelog [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads the tenant\(aqs change history, an audit log (personal data: who changed what, with the old and new values in \fB\-o json\fR), ordered by when the changes occurred. AT is when, TYPE create, update or delete, ENTITY and ENTITY ID the changed document (an order, customer, product, site, \[u2026]), ACTOR who changed it (a name, system, external or unknown) and FIELDS the changed fields. Without a lower bound on occurredAt (not only inside OR), Emporix returns the last 30 days, a window that moves while the pages are read: on an active tenant, read a closed range in the past, e.g. \fB\-\-query\fR \fB\(aqoccurredAt:(>"2026\-09\-01T00:00:00.000Z" AND <"2026\-10\-01T00:00:00.000Z")\(aq\fR, or use \fB\-\-limit\fR; otherwise a change can come or go between pages, so the read fails or misses it. One document\(aqs history: \fB\-\-query\fR \fB\(aqentity:order entityId:ID\(aq\fR.
.PP
Requires the changelog.changelog_read scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx changelog list"
List changes.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx changelog list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the tenant\(aqs change history, an audit log (personal data: who changed what, with the old and new values in \fB\-o json\fR), ordered by when the changes occurred. AT is when, TYPE create, update or delete, ENTITY and ENTITY ID the changed document (an order, customer, product, site, \[u2026]), ACTOR who changed it (a name, system, external or unknown) and FIELDS the changed fields. Without a lower bound on occurredAt (not only inside OR), Emporix returns the last 30 days, a window that moves while the pages are read: on an active tenant, read a closed range in the past, e.g. \fB\-\-query\fR \fB\(aqoccurredAt:(>"2026\-09\-01T00:00:00.000Z" AND <"2026\-10\-01T00:00:00.000Z")\(aq\fR, or use \fB\-\-limit\fR; otherwise a change can come or go between pages, so the read fails or misses it. One document\(aqs history: \fB\-\-query\fR \fB\(aqentity:order entityId:ID\(aq\fR.
.PP
Requires the changelog.changelog_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among AT, TYPE, ENTITY, ENTITY ID, NAME, ACTOR, FIELDS.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
